{
 "id": "corner-bracket-2020-petg",
 "brief": "An inside corner bracket joining two 2020 aluminium extrusions at a right angle, PETG on an FDM printer, printed flat so the layers stack along Z. One extrusion runs along X under the bracket (its face is the plane y = 0), the other runs up along Y beside it (its face is the plane x = 0). The bracket lives in x = 0 to 45, y = 0 to 45, z = -10 to 10. One M5 screw goes down (-Y) into a T-nut in the first extrusion at x = 30, z = 0, through a 6 mm thick foot; one M5 screw goes sideways (-X) into a T-nut in the second at y = 30, z = 0, through a 6 mm thick foot. The upright extrusion can be pushed 250 N along its own length, pulled 250 N straight off the bracket, or pushed 150 N sideways (along Z). Safety factor 2.5.",
